            "review_title": "Review at Vuon Nho Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Omer G\n20 contributions\n0\nTo order from the menu is like box of chocolate's - you never know what you gonna get\nFeb 2014 • Friends\nWe went to this restaurant because of the good reviews on trip advisor. But there was to much misunderstanding and wrong orderers. first of all, to read your bank account is easter then to read this menu. It has Vietnamese, Russian and English - all together.\nWe ordered \"mushroom & vegetables\", \"beef around the fire\", and \"mackerel fish with tomato souse\" - all we pointed and made sure the waiter understanding what we are asking. We specifically asked: not spicy! \n\nOne minute later the waiters coming to us and saying that the fish we asked is not available. We said OK and came with her to choose a different fish from the acourium. When they brought the fish to the table, we saw that they brought us the first fish ( the one that they said they don't have). 10 minutes later they brought us the second fish - although we thought its was clear that we wanted just one fish. We told them about it and they were sorry and took the second fish away. Beside that everything we ordered was very spicy - not like we asked.\n\nWhen we got the bill we saw that they charged us on two fishes, not one. We told the waiter about it and she corrected it, we gave her the money and she gave us less change then we deserved...so many mistakes in one bad meal...\nIf you still want to go We recommend the beer, its the only thing that they served right.\nRead more\nWritten February 23, 2014",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
